.TH GIT-RELEASE 1 "2026-07-29" "gitplus" "gitplus Manual"
.SH NAME
git-release \- tag the current commit and publish a GitHub release for it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git release
.I VERSION
[\fB\-\-notes\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.br
.B git release
\fB\-\-major\fR|\fB\-\-minor\fR|\fB\-\-patch\fR
[\fB\-\-notes\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.br
.B git release
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Automates the flow a GitHub release actually needs: an annotated tag, a push
of that tag, and
.BR "gh release create" .
.B git tag
+
.B "git push origin <tag>"
alone does
.B not
create a visible GitHub Release \(em that is a separate API call, which this
always makes, so a release never ends up silently half-finished (a real tag
with no Release to show for it).
.PP
The version can be given explicitly, or derived by bumping the latest
.I vX.Y.Z
tag with
.BR \-\-major / \-\-minor / \-\-patch .
Release notes can be given explicitly with
.BR \-\-notes ,
or left to
.BR "gh release create --generate-notes" ,
which summarizes PRs/commits since the last release. Both the version and
the notes are independently either automatic or manual.
.PP
Refuses to run with uncommitted changes (including untracked files \(em
checked with
.BR "git status --porcelain" ,
not a plain
.BR "git diff --quiet" ,
which misses them), or if the current branch has diverged from its origin
tracking branch: a release should tag something that is actually pushed, not
local-only work.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I VERSION
An explicit version, e.g.
.IR v1.3.0 .
Must look like
.IR vX.Y.Z .
.TP
.BR \-\-major ", " \-\-minor ", " \-\-patch
Bump the latest
.I vX.Y.Z
tag instead of naming a version explicitly. Requires at least one existing
tag matching that pattern.
.TP
.BR \-\-notes " " \fITEXT\fR
Use
.I TEXT
as the release notes instead of auto-generating them.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would happen and change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires the GitHub CLI
.RB ( gh ),
authenticated for the repository
.RB ( "gh auth login" ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git release v1.3.0
Tag and release an explicit version.
.TP
.B git release --patch
Bump the latest tag's patch version and release it.
.TP
.B git release --minor --notes "New git swap command"
Bump the minor version with hand-written release notes.
.TP
.B git release --major -n
Preview a major-version bump without changing anything.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-tag (1),
.BR gh-release (1)
